// Run-parity coverage for normalizeFoldedOperands's own multi-slot repair
// (src/backend/clr_emitter.cpp): a fold deficit of two or more, where every
// slot the repair reloads is itself folded, with no genuine value left on
// the real CIL evaluation stack between them. Each shape below gives its
// consumer a live sibling operand read directly alongside a match
// expression; Compiler::compileMatchBody (src/compiler.cpp) reserves one
// phantom local for that live sibling too, once a match sits inside a
// larger expression, so ADD, CALL, BUILD_LIST, and BUILD_MAP each face a
// consumer whose folded operands span more than one Lox slot at once.
//
// This file lives under clr-only/ for the same reason
// clr-only/31_deep_recursion.lox does: tools/diff_runtimes.py's CI probes
// step walks test/translation-probes/ non-recursively and diffs native
// against the JVM backend, and the JVM backend's own repair for this same
// mechanism refuses a deficit above one — every shape below would abort at
// JVM emit time, which is not a JVM regression to report. This file has no
// JVM twin; tools/check_clr_probes.sh names it directly for the CLR
// checkpoint.
//
// The last shape closes a second, distinct hazard the same multi-slot
// repair can hit: when two or more of the folded slots are ALSO captured
// by an inner closure, each one lowers through the captured-slot load an
// ordinary GET_LOCAL already uses, and that load emits a pair of ilasm
// labels keyed only by the consuming instruction's own offset. Two folded
// slots read at one offset need two distinct label pairs, not the same
// pair emitted twice.

// Shape 1: ADD, both operands folded — the live "1" and the match result
// share one consumer, and neither sits on the real evaluation stack once
// compileMatchBody folds the sibling alongside the match.
print 1 + match 1 { case 1 => 2 case _ => 3 };

// Shape 2: CALL, a folded argument with a live argument on each side of
// it — the callee stays genuine; every argument slot folds.
fun addThree(x, y, z) { return x + y + z; }
print addThree(1, match 1 { case 1 => 2 case _ => 3 }, 4);

// Shape 3: BUILD_LIST, a folded middle element with a live element on
// each side.
print [1, match 1 { case 1 => 2 case _ => 3 }, 4];

// Shape 4: BUILD_MAP, a folded value with a live key/value pair alongside
// it.
print {1: match 1 { case 1 => 2 case _ => 3 }, 3: 4};

// Shape 5: two folded slots that are ALSO captured-closure slots, so the
// multi-slot repair's own load routes through the captured-slot lowering
// twice at the same instruction offset.
fun outer() {
    {
        var p = 1;
        var q = 2;
        fun inner() { return p + q; }
        print inner();
    }
    print 1 + match 1 { case 1 => 2 case _ => 3 };
}
outer();
